1. Definitions

“Software” means the Euryphos source code, object code, and accompanying documentation in this repository, but only to the extent the Licensor has authority to license that material.

“Individual” means a natural person acting on their own behalf.

“Personal Use” means use solely by an Individual for that Individual’s own personal devices, household, home lab, hobby, or self-directed learning. Personal Use must not be performed for, on behalf of, or as part of the operations of a Company or Business, and must not provide services to customers or generate a commercial benefit for a Company or Business.

“Company or Business” means a company, corporation, partnership, limited liability company, sole-proprietorship, or other entity or operation organized to conduct trade, commerce, or for-profit business.

“Corporate Use” means any use of the Software by, for, or on behalf of a Company or Business. This includes managing or monitoring company or business computers, servers, endpoints, networks, or infrastructure; internal business operations; customer-facing services; consulting; managed services; and use by an employee, contractor, consultant, reseller, or service provider acting for a Company or Business. Corporate Use requires a separate written commercial license even if the deployment is internal or does not directly generate revenue.

“Licensor” means the copyright holder(s) or other rights holder(s) authorized to grant the applicable rights.

2. Free Personal Use Grant

Subject to this license, the Licensor grants an Individual a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free, non-transferable license to download, reproduce, compile, execute, and modify the Software solely for Personal Use.

No fee is charged for the Personal Use rights granted in this section.

3. Corporate Use Requires a Commercial License

The Personal Use grant does not authorize Corporate Use.

Before any Corporate Use, the user must obtain a separate written commercial license from the applicable rights holder. No commercial rights are granted by access to this repository, by possession of a copy, or by this Personal Use license.

Use by a person acting for a Company or Business is Corporate Use, even if that person downloads, installs, or operates the Software using a personal account or personal equipment.

4. Other Institutional Use

This license grants free rights only for Personal Use as defined above. It does not itself grant use rights to an institution or other legal entity. Situations involving public-sector, charitable, nonprofit, educational, or other institutional use that are not clearly Personal Use or Corporate Use require written permission or a separate written license from the applicable rights holder before deployment.

5. Restrictions

Except where a separate written agreement or applicable third-party license permits it, the licensee must not:
- use the Software for Corporate Use without a separate written commercial license;
- sell, rent, lease, sublicense, publish, or redistribute the Software or modified versions;
- make the Software available as a hosted, managed, or service-provider offering;
- remove or alter copyright, attribution, or license notices;
- circumvent technical restrictions or use the Software to violate applicable law.

An Individual may keep reasonable backup copies for that Individual’s Personal Use.

